{"school":{"dbn":"19K292","name":"J.H.S. 292 Margaret S. Douglas","boro":"Brooklyn","district":"19","district_label":"District 19","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"Middle","grades":"6 to 8","status":"open","enrollment":270,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"301 VERMONT STREET, BROOKLYN, NY 11207","phone":"718-688-7230 Ext 4512","website":null,"directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/middle-school/67944","accessibility":"Not Accessible","overview":"At Margaret S. Douglas JHS 292 we launch LEADERS! Our goal is to develop our scholars into leaders by providing them with quality education that prepares them for success in high school, college and beyond. Our teachers work collaboratively to ensure that students are provided instruction  based on their individual needs. We strive to meet the academic, cultural and social needs of our scholars by providing them with rigorous instruction in all content areas that is culturally relevant. In addition we engage in social emotional learning with restorative practices embedded throughout our community. We have a Specialized High School program offered to all students that gives them the opportunity to prepare for the the test and an opportunity to attend high schools with academic rigor that will prepare them to compete in an international market. Our seventh and eighth grade scholars are afforded the opportunity to prepare for and take Regents exams in Algebra 1; Living Environment; and US History and Government. Over 90% o9f our scholars who take regents exam pass with a 90% or higher rate which earns them accelerated high school credit. We also offer  performing arts classes such as  Dance, Martial Arts, Music/Band, Photography, and Film Making.","start_time":"08:19am","end_time":"02:39pm","languages":null,"subway":"3 to Pennsylvania Av; A, C to Van Siclen Av; J to Alabama Av; L to Sutter Av","bus":"B12, B14, B20, B25, B83, Q24, Q56","shared_building":"0","neighborhood":"East New York"